## One rule that exists ONLY for units: EVERY UNIT IS SELF-CONTAINED
Your `TestCase` runs after `TestSet.configure()` and after the previous case's own
`tear_down()`. Assume NOTHING another `TestCase` configured is still in effect when your
`main()` starts — only what `configure()` set up. If your step's action presumes a state
("with all optional TLVs now selected", "with the port already in the VLAN"), ESTABLISH that
state yourself in `main()` before you verify it, and undo it in your own `tear_down()`. Never
skip a precondition because an earlier step "already did it": it did, and then it was torn
down. On a real pass 6 of 38 units failed for exactly this reason and for no product reason.
